{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/FlatMap\/timeout(_:customError:)"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE7timeout_11customErrorAA14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutVy_x12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockVGs8DurationV_s0F0_pSgtF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7FlatMapV","modules":[{"name":"Afluent","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/TimeoutSequence.swift#L176","fileName":"TimeoutSequence.swift"},"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"16.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"16.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"16.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"16.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"9.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false}],"role":"symbol","title":"timeout(_:customError:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":")?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SuspendingClock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"code":"SuspendingClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/flatmap\/timeout(_:customerror:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuspendingClock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}]}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":") holds the one thread"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/FlatMap"]]},"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent","type":"top